  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2-2-PIM-New large public investment projects submitted to the Ministry of Economy (as part of the budget preparation) are screened, appraised and prioritized in compliance with government PIM guidance</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="0" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="50%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;The Prime Minister (PM) decree on approval of procedure and methodology for the identification, appraisal, prioritization, and evaluation of public investment projects has been developed in May 2021 (N 472-L). According to this decree information on all mediumand large size projects is being submitted to the Ministry of the Economy for screening and appraisal.&amp;nbsp;As of November 2021 there were 15 projects in the pipeline of which ten had gone through the quality assessment phase (of which 3 were large projects). Allten projects reviewed by the Ministry of Economy and Finance were returned to the relevant ministries&amp;nbsp;for review. &amp;nbsp;All are in the pre-appraisal stage. The&amp;nbsp;expected targets were not fully met; however, due to the ability to put in place a new PIM framework, including regulatory basis, guidelines and capacity building in almost all ministries and the start of the implementation of the framework, the progress assessed as:&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&amp;gt;&lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;em&amp;gt;&lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;u&amp;gt;Partially&amp;nbsp;Achieved.&lt;/u&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&amp;gt; &lt;/em&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/u&amp;gt;???????&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="50% +"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3-2-a-Justice Sector -Actions under Justice strategy have commenced and are on track.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="0/0" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="100/60">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;As of end 2020, 100 percent of the action items under the judicial sector strategy have commenced, with 33 percent having been completed and 64 percent partially completed. There have been substantial changes in the judicial code and the evaluation of judges has commenced.Indicator rvaluated as &lt;em&amp;gt;&lt;strong&amp;gt;Fully chieved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/em&amp;gt;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="100/ (33% completed and 64% partly completed)"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
