  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1-2-a-Customs Reforms: a)-Percentage of trucks that are scanned at the border, based on the risk assessment</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="100%" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="75%">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;A test program on risk-based inspections is being implemented at the Bagratashen customs post with Georgia. The final implementation delayed due to the end of customs infrastructure issues.&amp;nbsp;Therefore, because of infrastructure issues associated with the system, and not fully functioning of the advance declaration framework, the risk-based scanning system could not always be used.&amp;nbsp;???????&lt;em&amp;gt;&lt;strong&amp;gt;Not Achieved&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/em&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="Mostly 100%"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1-2-b- Agencies included in the National Single-window increased</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="3 agencies" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="12 agencies">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;Three state bodies are included in the newly established National Single Window, other agencies are under final testing tobe included in the system, however due to technical issues to be solved to allow full integration of all 17 agencies (14 state and 3 private), the full &amp;nbsp;results will be achieved with delay. While there were progress under this action but the indicator by thetime of assessment evaluated as &lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;em&amp;gt;Not&lt;em&amp;gt;&lt;strong&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/em&amp;gt;Achieved.&lt;/em&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="3 agencies"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3-3-Number of institutions included in the civil service performance management increased.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="40 institutions" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="60 institutions">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;The civil service unified system is introduced in all public agencies (68 agencies) and currently governed by the adopted laws except for local self-government bodies, the General Staff, the National Security Service, and the police. Indicator evaluated as &lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;em&amp;gt;Fully Achieved&amp;nbsp; and exceeded the target.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="68 institutions"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1-1-RIA-Number of laws and regulations with potential significant economic impact subject to RIA and timely public consultation increased.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="8" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="20">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Regulatory impact assessment procedures were adopted in December 2020. The methodology of RIAs established in January 2021.The responsible ministries adopted the criteria for determining the impact of regulatory initiatives.&amp;nbsp;After setting all new institutional arrangements, five initiatives are being piloted (completed) using the new procedures. According to December 2020 Government decree, it is planned that all drafts with possible significant impacts to be submitted to PM office accompanied by RIA starting December 2021. &amp;nbsp;While less RIAs were completed under the new system compared to the target due to the need to adopt the legal and institutional basis for the start of the reform, the adopted framework envisages full roll-out of RIA as of December 2021; hence, the progress and results are assessed as: ???????&lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;em&amp;gt;Partially Achieved.&lt;/em&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;??????&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="5"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1-3-State aid database is functional, published, and used to monitor granted aid.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-10-31" value="No available information" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-10-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Database is functional">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;The Law on &amp;ldquo;Protection of Economic Competition&amp;rdquo; was amended in January 2020 and clarified the concept of state aid and required registration of state aid. Government decree adopted in May 2021 (N 784) and Competition Protection Commission (CPC) decree in June 2020 (228-L) has defined the procedures, format, and deadlines for providing the CPC with information on state aid. After institutional foundation being in pace the CPC is being provided with information on state aid on a continuous basis. As of October 2021, the database is not ready to go live but will do so by the end of 2021. Indicator evaluated as &amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;em&amp;gt;Substantially Achieved. &lt;/em&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&amp;gt;????????????&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="Database is functional but not publicby the deadline."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3-2-b)- Share of small claim cases eligible for the small claims procedure inc increased.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2019-12-31" year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="10 p.p. increase">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;???????There has been a decrease in number of eligible civil cases to which streamlined minor claims procedures have been applied in 2020. (Note: Simplified procedures are related to monetary obligations.) The decrease explained by the introduction of a numberof mitigation measures for businesses and citizens impacted by the lockdown and Covid19 restrictions, including exemption of certain obligations, extension of period for fulfillment of obligations, review of timelines for obligations, etc. &amp;nbsp;Also, a large number of court trials were postponed. As the result, fewer cases on violation of monetary obligations were filed and proceeded in the courts, resulting in a smaller share in total of cases. The achievment assessed as&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;em&amp;gt;Substantially Achieved. &lt;/em&amp;gt;???????&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="15 percentage point decrease."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
 </iati-activity>
